An Example Data of Biomedicine Task B (Baseline). Question: Which of the following is not a tumor suppressor gene? Candidates: (1) pRb;
(2) p16;
(3) PTCH;
(4) c-erbB1. B+T (Truthful Augmentation). Added premise: Tumor suppressor genes generally restrain cell proliferation or maintain
cellular integrity, whereas growth-promoting signaling genes can have
oncogenic functions when abnormally activated. B+H (Hallucinated Augmentation; Rule Contradiction). Added premise: c-erbB1 is a tumor suppressor gene because all genes involved in cell
signaling can suppress tumor growth under certain conditions.

